  "story": {
    "language": "en",
    "translationLanguage": "zh-Hant",
    "textEn": "In art class, my friend and I want to create a colorful garden picture for the wall. We look at the flower on our table and notice the shape of each leaf. I use a crayon to draw a house on my paper, then color the roof and the grass. There is a pencil in the cup if I need to plan another line before adding color. My friend can cut a round shape while I make room for a yellow sun above the house. We put a little glue from the bottle on the circle and put it on the picture. A square piece of paper can become another window, and a brush with paint can add flowers. We work with care and leave space between the flowers, so the garden does not feel too crowded. When we finish, we stand back together and smile at our beautiful garden.",
    "textZh": "在美術課上，朋友和我想創作一幅色彩豐富的花園圖畫，放在牆上。我們看看桌上的花朵，注意每片葉子的形狀。我用蠟筆在紙上畫一間房屋，接著替屋頂和草地塗色。如果我需要先規劃另一條線再上色，杯子裡有一支鉛筆可用。朋友剪一個圓形，我則在房屋上方留位置給黃色的太陽。我們從瓶子裡取一點膠水抹在圓紙上，把它壓貼在圖畫上。一張正方形紙可以變成另一扇窗，畫筆沾顏料後則能加上花朵。我們小心地做，在花朵之間留空間，讓花園不會太擠。完成後，我們一起退後看看，對著漂亮的花園微笑。",
